ns 2 of the 32 cells uphill («chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -32 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -5 mV), and at its octahedral literature value (-300 mV) 5, an upper count («chloro (device, programmatic)» at MMFF geometries, electronic (32) → -45 mV; «chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -82 mV; «chloro + 1 H₂O on Cl⁻» at relaxed, electronic → -18 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at MMFF geometries, electronic (32) → -18 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -55 mV); the alternative 4.44 V convention (-159 mV) alone 0, with spin–orbit coupling 10 ⊥ 12 (the [Os(bipy)₃] ⊥ octahedral value); against the measured free flavin the spin–orbit-shifted device couple lies at +70 ⊥ +20 mV — so with spin–orbit coupling at either value the protocol does not determine the sign of the device cascade."
